1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,159
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:20,214 --> 00:01:22,047
♪ ♪

5
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:57,182
♪ ♪

6
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:34,019
That jeep right there,
that's your rental.

7
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:38,990
You have a good stay.

8
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,859
Spencer Hamilton?

9
00:03:14,928 --> 00:03:16,661
That's right.

10
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:17,896
Ed Tucker.

11
00:03:17,964 --> 00:03:20,399
Everything's set.

12
00:03:20,467 --> 00:03:24,002
Power's on, water's
on, phone works.

13
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:25,737
You need a key?

14
00:03:25,806 --> 00:03:27,171
Got one.

15
00:03:29,175 --> 00:03:30,353
What's that?

16
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:31,443
My bill.

17
00:03:31,512 --> 00:03:33,077
Your brother always
paid me in cash.

18
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:34,245
Oh.

19
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:36,180
Yeah, he'd usually
pay me when I got done.

20
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:37,816
That way neither
one of us forgot.

21
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:39,165
That's a good idea.

22
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:41,152
I was wondering when
somebody would come down

23
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,554
to close the house.

24
00:03:42,623 --> 00:03:44,322
You gonna sell it?

25
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:46,090
I don't know.

26
00:03:46,159 --> 00:03:47,659
I wouldn't park my car there.

27
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:51,029
We cut a limb off that tree.

28
00:03:51,098 --> 00:03:52,730
It drips sap on everything.

29
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:54,977
Do you know where
my brother was killed?

30
00:03:55,001 --> 00:03:56,033
Yeah.

31
00:03:56,102 --> 00:03:57,335
Will you show me?

32
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:59,705
Yeah.

33
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:16,621
Out there?

34
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:18,022
What is that?

35
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:19,291
A duck blind?

36
00:04:19,359 --> 00:04:20,392
Yeah.

37
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,893
Season's been over six months.

38
00:04:21,962 --> 00:04:24,863
How'd it happen?

39
00:04:24,932 --> 00:04:28,800
Well, the way I heard
it, Frank was in the boat.

40
00:04:28,869 --> 00:04:30,913
His four buddies was
already in that blind.

41
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:34,873
A bunch of ducks come
in flying low, you know,

42
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,952
and Frank grabbed
his gun, stood up

43
00:04:36,976 --> 00:04:38,976
just as his friend fired.

44
00:04:39,045 --> 00:04:41,324
Hit Frank square in the chest.

45
00:04:41,348 --> 00:04:43,181
Frank was in the boat?

46
00:04:43,249 --> 00:04:44,527
That's right.

47
00:04:44,551 --> 00:04:48,119
Heard he was setting decoys.

48
00:04:48,188 --> 00:04:49,521
You can ask the sheriff.

49
00:04:49,589 --> 00:04:51,289
It's what all the fellas said...

50
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:53,836
You know, the ones
that was there. Yeah.

51
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:55,939
Anyway, like I said,
your brother always

52
00:04:55,963 --> 00:04:57,162
paid me cash.

53
00:04:57,230 --> 00:04:59,150
That way neither
one of us forgot.

54
00:05:02,369 --> 00:05:04,870
I ain't never seen
nothing like it.

55
00:05:04,938 --> 00:05:07,305
Them big blues got
them schools of trout

56
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:09,152
and run 'em up on the beach

57
00:05:09,176 --> 00:05:11,120
and I picked up two or
three bucketfuls myself.

58
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,288
When was that?

59
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,312
Yesterday.

60
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,046
I always miss it.

61
00:05:15,115 --> 00:05:16,748
It never fails.

62
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:19,517
I get there the day
before it or the day after.

63
00:05:19,586 --> 00:05:21,753
It just kills my soul.

64
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,599
Wouldn't you think a
person just one time

65
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:25,168
could get there the day of it?

66
00:05:25,192 --> 00:05:26,602
Happens to me, too.

67
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:28,672
Boys, and that's what
brought the people down here.

68
00:05:28,696 --> 00:05:33,898
The fish, water, beaches,
sun, lost colony play.

69
00:05:33,967 --> 00:05:36,935
In the '50s, that was just fine,

70
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:39,036
but now we just
got too many of 'em.

71
00:05:39,106 --> 00:05:40,550
Tell, 'em, Commissioner.

72
00:05:40,574 --> 00:05:42,273
Wintertime...

73
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:43,641
Good for the economy.

74
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:45,521
Let's people know
where this place is at.

75
00:05:45,545 --> 00:05:46,611
Good all around.

76
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,713
You campaigning
again, Commissioner?

77
00:05:49,783 --> 00:05:51,816
I might.

78
00:05:51,885 --> 00:05:53,696
I voted for you last time.

79
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,820
Me, too.

80
00:05:55,889 --> 00:05:57,567
I voted for you when
you ran democrat,

81
00:05:57,591 --> 00:05:59,602
when you ran republican
and when you ran independent.

82
00:05:59,626 --> 00:06:00,859
You did?

83
00:06:00,927 --> 00:06:02,593
No, but Mama did.

84
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,241
Said she felt sorry for you.

85
00:06:06,265 --> 00:06:09,233
Well, honey, you just tell
Mama to keep on voting.

86
00:06:09,302 --> 00:06:10,969
Keep on feeling
sorry for old Gordon,

87
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,104
but keep on voting.

88
00:06:13,172 --> 00:06:15,874
Hell, Commissioner,
if you ever win,

89
00:06:15,943 --> 00:06:17,787
we'll have to get out
the high school band

90
00:06:17,811 --> 00:06:19,177
and have a parade.

91
00:06:23,984 --> 00:06:27,886
I'm Spencer Hamilton,
Frank Hamilton's brother.

92
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:31,089
Oh... Oh, uh, have a seat.

93
00:06:31,158 --> 00:06:35,393
I'm Gordon Lewis.

94
00:06:35,461 --> 00:06:36,539
Commissioner?

95
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:39,130
It's a little joke.

96
00:06:39,199 --> 00:06:40,532
Have something.

97
00:06:40,601 --> 00:06:42,233
Did you know my brother?

98
00:06:42,302 --> 00:06:46,137
Well, yeah, I knew him.

99
00:06:46,206 --> 00:06:49,974
You know, it's interesting
that you should come up to me.

100
00:06:50,043 --> 00:06:52,076
I've got this little law office.

101
00:06:52,145 --> 00:06:54,045
Don't practice much anymore.

102
00:06:54,114 --> 00:06:55,958
I got a little
insurance business,

103
00:06:55,982 --> 00:06:58,349
sell some real estate
from time to time.

104
00:06:58,418 --> 00:07:00,685
But I did do a couple
things for your brother.

105
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:03,555
Um, so yeah, I
knew... Who killed him?

106
00:07:03,624 --> 00:07:06,992
Well, you know,
that was an accident.

107
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,192
Happened last November.

108
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,794
I've been stationed in Europe.

109
00:07:09,863 --> 00:07:11,295
I just mustered out.

110
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:16,201
So, uh, you want to
step over to my little office

111
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:17,636
and go through Frank's papers...

112
00:07:17,704 --> 00:07:18,937
What I got of 'em?

113
00:07:19,006 --> 00:07:21,566
All I want is the name of
the man who killed him.

114
00:07:23,209 --> 00:07:26,344
Well, uh...

115
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:27,779
Dalton.

116
00:07:27,848 --> 00:07:29,781
Here's the man
you ought to talk to.

117
00:07:31,651 --> 00:07:34,018
Spencer Hamilton...
Frank Hamilton's brother.

118
00:07:34,087 --> 00:07:35,653
Sheriff Parks.

119
00:07:35,722 --> 00:07:38,022
Oh, it's a pleasure to
meet you, Mr. Hamilton.

120
00:07:38,091 --> 00:07:39,802
Sorry about your brother.

121
00:07:39,826 --> 00:07:41,259
Who killed him?

122
00:07:41,327 --> 00:07:42,627
Well, it was an accident.

123
00:07:42,696 --> 00:07:44,195
Who pulled the trigger?

124
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:50,068
A man named Ryan Bartell.

125
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:51,502
You know where I can find him?

126
00:07:51,571 --> 00:07:53,370
Well, haven't seen
him, or his friends.

127
00:07:53,439 --> 00:07:54,639
I hear they're in town.

128
00:07:54,708 --> 00:07:58,609
I know how you must
feel, but it was an accident.

129
00:07:58,679 --> 00:08:00,211
You seem awfully upset.

130
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,548
I hope you don't feel...
You don't know how I feel.

131
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:16,928
Thanks.

132
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:18,440
You here for the fishing?

133
00:08:18,464 --> 00:08:20,031
Yeah, I've heard the blue fish

134
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,933
run the trout right
up into your bunk.

135
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:23,046
That's right.

136
00:08:23,070 --> 00:08:24,602
Been here long?

137
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:25,849
Born here.

138
00:08:25,873 --> 00:08:27,539
Where you from?

139
00:08:27,607 --> 00:08:29,407
Where it snows.

140
00:08:29,476 --> 00:08:31,209
Ooh.

141
00:08:31,278 --> 00:08:33,578
Ryan Bartell, uh, you know him?

142
00:08:33,647 --> 00:08:35,113
Oh, yeah. Comes in here

143
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,348
all the time with his buddies.

144
00:08:37,417 --> 00:08:39,050
Known Ryan long?

145
00:08:39,119 --> 00:08:41,185
No. Friend of a friend.

146
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:42,565
Yeah, well, he is a card.

147
00:08:42,589 --> 00:08:46,057
Loves to party, but he's
got a hell of a temper.

148
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:47,358
That right?

149
00:08:47,427 --> 00:08:49,271
Oh, yeah. One night last year,

150
00:08:49,295 --> 00:08:51,896
Ryan comes in
here with his pals.

151
00:08:51,965 --> 00:08:55,033
And all of a sudden,
Ryan gets into a brawl

152
00:08:55,101 --> 00:08:56,434
with one of his friends...

153
00:08:56,503 --> 00:08:58,848
A guy by the name
of Frank Hamilton,

154
00:08:58,872 --> 00:09:00,371
over some girl.

155
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:03,374
Ryan wants her, she wants Frank.

156
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:05,409
Just an argument over a girl?

157
00:09:05,478 --> 00:09:06,956
Oh, yeah, well, it happens.

158
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,413
But it got settled.

159
00:09:08,481 --> 00:09:11,115
Another girl comes in.

160
00:09:11,184 --> 00:09:13,744
Now speak of the
devil. There they are.

161
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:20,892
Some beer all around.

162
00:09:20,961 --> 00:09:22,693
Coming right up.

163
00:09:34,508 --> 00:09:37,309
I'm Spencer Hamilton...

164
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:40,078
Frank Hamilton's brother.

165
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,362
I'm Ernie D'Amato.

166
00:09:46,386 --> 00:09:47,663
This is David
Channing, Ryan Bartell,

167
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:49,753
and Lee Kramer.

168
00:09:52,058 --> 00:09:53,669
You want something else?

169
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,593
No.

170
00:09:55,662 --> 00:09:56,761
We're really, really sorry

171
00:09:56,830 --> 00:09:58,295
about what happened to Frank.

172
00:09:58,365 --> 00:10:00,231
Yeah, he, uh...

173
00:10:00,299 --> 00:10:01,766
Frank-Frank was a great guy.

174
00:10:01,835 --> 00:10:03,034
He was a great guy.

175
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:05,737
What about you?

176
00:10:05,806 --> 00:10:08,840
How sorry are you?

177
00:10:08,909 --> 00:10:10,809
I'm sorry.

178
00:10:10,877 --> 00:10:12,343
It was an accident.

179
00:10:12,412 --> 00:10:13,590
What happened, happened.

180
00:10:13,614 --> 00:10:15,513
And that's it?

181
00:10:15,582 --> 00:10:16,759
It was an accident.

182
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:17,860
Ask anybody.

183
00:10:17,884 --> 00:10:22,720
I'm asking you.

184
00:10:22,789 --> 00:10:25,390
Why'd you kill my brother?

185
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,270
I told you, it was an accident.

186
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,826
Frank was in the boat

187
00:10:28,895 --> 00:10:30,127
when you shot him, right?

188
00:10:30,197 --> 00:10:32,530
Right?

189
00:10:32,599 --> 00:10:34,477
He gave his
statement to the sheriff.

190
00:10:34,501 --> 00:10:35,934
Frank was in the boat?

191
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,435
Yeah, he was in the boat.

192
00:10:37,503 --> 00:10:38,503
You're a liar.

193
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,707
Ryan, the man lost his brother.

194
00:10:42,776 --> 00:10:44,020
You calling me a liar?

195
00:10:44,044 --> 00:10:45,388
Yeah, you're a liar.

196
00:10:45,412 --> 00:10:47,311
Frank wasn't in any boat.

197
00:10:47,381 --> 00:10:49,124
He almost drowned
when he was three.

198
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:51,549
He had hydrophobia.

199
00:10:51,618 --> 00:10:55,086
He wouldn't go near the water.

200
00:10:56,590 --> 00:10:59,323
You murdered my brother.

201
00:10:59,392 --> 00:11:01,559
Liar!

202
00:11:15,809 --> 00:11:17,141
Hey! Hey, cut it out!

203
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:18,287
Back off!

204
00:11:18,311 --> 00:11:19,944
Now tell me why you
murdered my brother!

205
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:21,980
Hey, drop the knife.

206
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:26,417
Drop the knife.

207
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:42,745
All right, what's going on here?

208
00:11:42,769 --> 00:11:45,370
Ask him.

209
00:11:49,576 --> 00:11:52,010
I didn't start it.

210
00:11:52,078 --> 00:11:54,245
You better hold it together.

211
00:12:02,822 --> 00:12:04,655
That was real dumb.

212
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:07,224
Hey, damn it, I didn't start it.

213
00:12:12,165 --> 00:12:13,531
We got a problem.

214
00:12:13,599 --> 00:12:14,933
Oh, yeah.

215
00:12:28,881 --> 00:12:31,682
Take a die and don't look
at it until you get home.

216
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:33,329
If it's white, you go to bed.

217
00:12:33,353 --> 00:12:35,086
If it's red,

218
00:12:35,155 --> 00:12:36,554
you've got work to do.

219
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:39,791
And it has to be done by
7:00 a.m. Are we agreed?

220
00:13:12,826 --> 00:13:16,995
Nobody talks to anybody,
including each other

221
00:13:17,063 --> 00:13:18,996
until after 9:00 a.m.

222
00:13:21,568 --> 00:13:23,412
Only the man that does the job

223
00:13:23,436 --> 00:13:25,996
will know that he did it.

224
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:40,818
Yeah?

225
00:13:40,886 --> 00:13:44,455
What for?

226
00:13:44,523 --> 00:13:48,459
Yeah, yeah, okay.

227
00:13:48,527 --> 00:13:50,594
I'll be there!

228
00:14:23,163 --> 00:14:25,963
Hey, what the hell
took you so long?

229
00:15:25,325 --> 00:15:26,325
Morning.

230
00:15:26,359 --> 00:15:27,291
Morning.

231
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:30,093
Show him the warrant, Clarence.

232
00:15:35,035 --> 00:15:37,502
Floyd Tubbs... he
owns the barbershop...

233
00:15:37,570 --> 00:15:40,170
Was out walking in
the woods this morning

234
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,840
about a mile from here, 6:00.

235
00:15:42,908 --> 00:15:45,209
Heard pistol shots,
and went to look.

236
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:48,312
Ryan Bartell was lying there
with two bullets through him,

237
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:51,048
stone dead.

238
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:54,051
Wait a minute. I
don't even own a gun.

239
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,330
And I wasn't out running around

240
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:56,565
in the woods at 6:00.

241
00:15:56,589 --> 00:15:58,021
I was right here.

242
00:15:58,091 --> 00:16:00,002
Yeah? Yeah. Handing a mechanic

243
00:16:00,026 --> 00:16:01,626
the keys to that car over there.

244
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:03,328
He came to fix the ignition.

245
00:16:03,396 --> 00:16:05,196
At 6:00 in the morning?

246
00:16:05,265 --> 00:16:06,975
He said he was real busy.
His work was backed up

247
00:16:06,999 --> 00:16:08,711
and that was the only
time he could fix it.

248
00:16:08,735 --> 00:16:10,975
What's his name? Jack.

249
00:16:12,372 --> 00:16:13,303
Jack something.

250
00:16:13,373 --> 00:16:14,304
Go call Jack Rose.

251
00:16:14,374 --> 00:16:15,639
Yes, sir.

252
00:16:17,877 --> 00:16:19,543
Sheriff.

253
00:16:19,612 --> 00:16:23,380
Why are you looking at me?

254
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:27,050
Found this in the gun case.

255
00:16:28,755 --> 00:16:31,122
Recently fired.

256
00:16:31,191 --> 00:16:33,457
Wait a minute.

257
00:16:33,526 --> 00:16:35,826
I've never seen that before.

258
00:16:35,895 --> 00:16:38,061
Jack Rose said he
hadn't been anywhere near

259
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:39,241
this place this morning!

260
00:16:39,265 --> 00:16:41,132
What?!

261
00:16:41,201 --> 00:16:42,466
Let's go, Mr. Hamilton.

262
00:16:42,535 --> 00:16:45,503
This is crazy. I
didn't kill anybody.

263
00:16:48,575 --> 00:16:49,707
<i>I hereby grant</i>

264
00:16:49,776 --> 00:16:52,376
the defense's motion,
and in so doing,

265
00:16:52,444 --> 00:16:56,013
find the prosecution's
case against Horton Garrett

266
00:16:56,082 --> 00:17:00,051
to be solely lacking
in substance and merit.

267
00:17:00,119 --> 00:17:02,987
I therefore order that the
charges against Mr. Garrett

268
00:17:03,056 --> 00:17:05,489
be dropped and that he
be released immediately.

269
00:17:05,558 --> 00:17:08,025
Court is adjourned.

270
00:17:10,329 --> 00:17:11,606
Thank you, Mr. Matlock.

271
00:17:11,630 --> 00:17:12,910
Thank you a million times!

272
00:17:12,965 --> 00:17:14,298
Ah, just doing my job.

273
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:16,033
Now you and your
wife go celebrate.

274
00:17:16,102 --> 00:17:17,734
We will. Oh, we will!

275
00:17:17,803 --> 00:17:18,902
Yeah.

276
00:17:23,909 --> 00:17:25,008
Where's Mr. Garrett?

277
00:17:25,077 --> 00:17:26,188
Free man.

278
00:17:26,212 --> 00:17:27,712
Free is right.

279
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:32,149
We just got this from the bank.

280
00:17:32,218 --> 00:17:34,385
His check bounced?!

281
00:17:34,454 --> 00:17:36,320
Hey, Mr. Garrett!

282
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:37,988
Excuse me. Excuse me.

283
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:39,201
Hey, Mr. Garrett!

284
00:17:39,225 --> 00:17:42,660
Just let me by.
Hey, Mr. Garrett!

285
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:43,761
Hey, fella!

286
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:54,705
I hate that.

287
00:17:54,774 --> 00:17:57,174
I hate that!

288
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:58,876
Don't you just hate that?

289
00:17:58,944 --> 00:18:01,223
We should only
take cash in advance.

290
00:18:01,247 --> 00:18:02,247
Yeah.

291
00:18:03,483 --> 00:18:05,816
Ben Matlock.

292
00:18:05,885 --> 00:18:07,585
Yes, sir, General.

293
00:18:07,654 --> 00:18:12,356
Uh, well, it's good to hear
your voice, General Colvin.

294
00:18:12,425 --> 00:18:14,992
It's been such a long time.

295
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:16,994
Uh-huh.

296
00:18:18,164 --> 00:18:21,865
Uh-huh. Uh, uh-huh.

297
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:25,703
Oh, well, sure.
Sure, I remember.

298
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,305
And, and...

299
00:18:27,373 --> 00:18:30,408
Why, yes, sir, yes, sir, I'd
be, I'd be glad to do that.

300
00:18:30,476 --> 00:18:32,176
Of course.

301
00:18:32,244 --> 00:18:35,780
Yes, sir. Bye, General Colvin.

302
00:18:35,848 --> 00:18:37,982
Hey, Michelle,

303
00:18:38,051 --> 00:18:40,617
you know who that was?

304
00:18:40,686 --> 00:18:43,921
General Colvin,
four-star general.

305
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:45,956
Big man. He did me a favor

306
00:18:46,025 --> 00:18:48,559
several years ago,
and now it's my turn.

307
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:52,262
Have you ever heard of town
called Manteo on Roanoke Island

308
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:53,865
in North Carolina?

309
00:19:25,798 --> 00:19:27,464
Mr. Matlock.

310
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:29,400
Yeah?

311
00:19:29,468 --> 00:19:30,579
You're supposed to go straight

312
00:19:30,603 --> 00:19:33,270
to the courthouse,
sir. They sent a cab.

313
00:19:36,108 --> 00:19:37,952
I've been in elevators
bigger than that.

314
00:19:37,976 --> 00:19:39,976
That thing bounced
like jackrabbit

315
00:19:40,045 --> 00:19:41,523
all the way from Raleigh.

316
00:19:41,547 --> 00:19:43,347
Well, at least you're
in good hands.

317
00:19:43,416 --> 00:19:45,949
Chris there is the most
experienced pilot we've got.

318
00:20:05,804 --> 00:20:07,971
Thanks, Roy.

319
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,040
Are you him?

320
00:20:10,109 --> 00:20:11,208
Him who?

321
00:20:11,277 --> 00:20:12,877
That lawyer. What lawyer?

322
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:14,757
The one they sent
for from Atlanta.

323
00:20:14,781 --> 00:20:18,148
Well, I'm a lawyer.

324
00:20:18,218 --> 00:20:20,751
We heard about your suit.

325
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,352
What suit?

326
00:20:22,422 --> 00:20:26,790
Is that it?

327
00:20:26,859 --> 00:20:28,925
Well, it's my suit.

328
00:20:28,994 --> 00:20:30,761
Excuse me.

329
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:32,863
That's him.

330
00:20:32,931 --> 00:20:33,997
That's him!

331
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,501
What do you think?

332
00:20:40,273 --> 00:20:42,833
He's supposed to be here.

333
00:20:46,045 --> 00:20:47,143
Mr. Matlock?

334
00:20:47,213 --> 00:20:49,113
Yeah.

335
00:20:49,182 --> 00:20:50,514
Glad to see ya.

336
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:52,716
I'm Gordon Lewis,
your co-counsel.

337
00:20:52,785 --> 00:20:54,017
Well, not really co-counsel.

338
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:56,367
I was kinda holding down
the fort till you got here.

339
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:57,788
This is Spencer Hamilton.

340
00:20:57,856 --> 00:20:58,900
Thanks for coming.

341
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:01,659
Oh, uh-huh, uh-huh. Well, uh...

342
00:21:01,727 --> 00:21:03,260
Ooh, we better get inside.

343
00:21:05,864 --> 00:21:10,101
Uh, Your Honor, Your
Honor, I'm-I'm sorry I'm late.

344
00:21:10,169 --> 00:21:12,135
Mr. Matlock, this is a pleasure!

345
00:21:12,205 --> 00:21:13,704
I'm Melissa Lyle,

346
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:15,472
and I have followed your career

347
00:21:15,541 --> 00:21:16,541
with great admiration!

348
00:21:16,576 --> 00:21:17,508
Oh, thank you.

349
00:21:17,577 --> 00:21:20,811
Uh, Your Honor, at this time...

350
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,012
Why are you late?

351
00:21:22,081 --> 00:21:23,914
I just got here.

352
00:21:23,983 --> 00:21:26,528
There's a big crowd
outside. I got stuck.

353
00:21:26,552 --> 00:21:28,497
I will not have that
crowd disrupting this trial,

354
00:21:28,521 --> 00:21:29,521
you understand?

355
00:21:29,589 --> 00:21:30,721
Well, yes, sir, but...

356
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:31,722
Good.

357
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,591
Now, in your absence,

358
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:37,327
your co-counsel, the prosecutor
and I have discussed bail.

359
00:21:37,397 --> 00:21:39,529
And it has been agreed

360
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:40,709
that $50,000 is reasonable.

361
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:42,177
You have no objections,
do you, Mr. Matlock?

362
00:21:42,201 --> 00:21:45,113
I was just holding
down the fort.

363
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,436
I'm not really co-counsel.

364
00:21:46,505 --> 00:21:49,272
Uh, no objection.

365
00:21:49,342 --> 00:21:51,909
Good. Mrs. Lyle,
anything further?

366
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:52,978
Oh, no, Your Honor.

367
00:21:53,012 --> 00:21:54,344
Fine. Mr. Matlock,

368
00:21:54,414 --> 00:21:57,013
if you'll sign on for the
case, we're in business.

369
00:21:57,083 --> 00:21:59,450
Court's adjourned.

370
00:22:04,423 --> 00:22:05,889
Okay.

371
00:22:07,093 --> 00:22:08,425
Well...

372
00:22:11,363 --> 00:22:12,963
Uh...

373
00:22:28,381 --> 00:22:29,747
Excuse me.

374
00:22:33,586 --> 00:22:34,885
You got a problem?

375
00:22:34,954 --> 00:22:36,465
You paid Jack Rose to lie.

376
00:22:36,489 --> 00:22:37,489
You're nuts, mister.

377
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:38,867
What the hell are
you talking about?

378
00:22:38,891 --> 00:22:40,290
Which one of you killed Ryan?

379
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:41,837
Or was it all of ya?

380
00:22:41,861 --> 00:22:43,739
Spencer! Get away from the car.

381
00:22:43,763 --> 00:22:45,596
Get away from the car.

382
00:22:45,665 --> 00:22:46,963
Spencer!

383
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:49,900
Murderers!

384
00:23:01,647 --> 00:23:03,926
You know a lot a
of people down here

385
00:23:03,950 --> 00:23:05,715
think you're guilty.

386
00:23:05,784 --> 00:23:09,186
That, that thing you
pulled on the street,

387
00:23:09,255 --> 00:23:12,289
that was dumb. I'm
talking real dumb.

388
00:23:12,358 --> 00:23:16,327
I never heard of
Roanoke Island before.

389
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:18,273
And the only reason
I'm down here now is

390
00:23:18,297 --> 00:23:21,765
General Colvin called
me and I owe him a favor.

391
00:23:21,834 --> 00:23:25,002
He said you were
one of his best men

392
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:26,881
and you had a hot temper.

393
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,538
Now I'm gonna warn you.

394
00:23:28,607 --> 00:23:30,652
During the course of this trial,

395
00:23:30,676 --> 00:23:32,620
you be one of the best men.

396
00:23:32,644 --> 00:23:35,245
Forget the hot temper part.

397
00:23:35,314 --> 00:23:36,325
You got that?

398
00:23:36,349 --> 00:23:39,116
Yeah.

399
00:23:39,185 --> 00:23:40,584
Okay.

400
00:23:40,652 --> 00:23:43,586
So, uh,

401
00:23:43,656 --> 00:23:45,656
this is where he was killed?

402
00:23:45,725 --> 00:23:46,768
What's his name?

403
00:23:46,792 --> 00:23:48,391
Ryan Bartell.

404
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:50,894
Killed Frank over some girl.

405
00:23:50,963 --> 00:23:52,529
Yeah? Yeah.

406
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:54,998
Were you and Frank close?

407
00:23:55,067 --> 00:23:56,567
We're actually pretty different,

408
00:23:56,635 --> 00:23:57,901
except for our temper.

409
00:23:57,970 --> 00:24:01,905
What'd he do for a living?

410
00:24:01,974 --> 00:24:04,407
He wheeled and
dealed in a lot of stuff.

411
00:24:04,476 --> 00:24:07,077
Did pretty well, I guess.

412
00:24:12,050 --> 00:24:14,484
We just started
patching things up.

413
00:24:17,022 --> 00:24:20,324
How do you suppose
that gun got in your house?

414
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:23,560
I don't know.

415
00:24:23,629 --> 00:24:25,429
But you were home?

416
00:24:25,497 --> 00:24:27,331
Yeah, the whole time.

417
00:24:27,399 --> 00:24:29,999
This mechanic, Jack
Rose, was there from...

418
00:24:30,068 --> 00:24:33,337
6:00 to 7:30 fixing the car.

419
00:24:33,405 --> 00:24:37,307
He told the sheriff
he was home in bed.

420
00:24:37,376 --> 00:24:38,642
Hm.

421
00:24:39,911 --> 00:24:42,378
Wonder why he lied.

422
00:24:44,851 --> 00:24:46,416
There you go, Jack
Rose's statement.

423
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:49,720
Oh, long as we're at it, why
don't I give you a copy of this, too.

424
00:24:49,788 --> 00:24:51,488
It's Conrad
McMasters' statement.

425
00:24:51,557 --> 00:24:54,958
Okay. Who's Conrad McMasters?

426
00:24:55,027 --> 00:24:56,027
Me.

427
00:24:56,094 --> 00:24:58,728
Conrad broke up a fight
between Ryan Bartell

428
00:24:58,798 --> 00:25:00,776
and your client the
day before the murder.

429
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:02,600
How?

430
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:05,569
Had my pistol.

431
00:25:05,638 --> 00:25:07,904
That's all there was to
it? Yeah, pretty much.

432
00:25:07,974 --> 00:25:11,208
Spencer Hamilton stuck
the knife in the table and left.

433
00:25:11,277 --> 00:25:12,643
There was a knife?

434
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:14,678
Yeah. Belonged to Ryan Bartell.

435
00:25:14,747 --> 00:25:16,491
Spencer had taken
it away from him,

436
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:19,015
and they got to
rassling about it, and...

437
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:21,952
Anyway, Ryan said he
didn't... he didn't start it.

438
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:24,654
Actually, they were both
pretty mad at each other, but...

439
00:25:24,724 --> 00:25:26,856
But you had your pistol. Yeah.

440
00:25:26,926 --> 00:25:30,327
Yeah, when I'm in
uniform, I have my pistol.

441
00:25:30,396 --> 00:25:31,562
That was good work.

442
00:25:31,631 --> 00:25:32,963
Thanks.

443
00:25:33,032 --> 00:25:35,098
Um...

444
00:25:35,167 --> 00:25:37,835
Ryan Bartell lives, uh,

445
00:25:37,904 --> 00:25:40,904
on the, uh, Mother
Vineyard Road.

446
00:25:40,973 --> 00:25:42,038
Sheriff?

447
00:25:42,108 --> 00:25:44,308
Well, why don't
you give Mr. Matlock

448
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:45,876
a ride out there.

449
00:25:45,945 --> 00:25:48,023
All right!

450
00:25:48,047 --> 00:25:50,213
My first name's Ben.

451
00:25:50,282 --> 00:25:51,381
Conrad.

452
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:52,916
B and C, Ben and Conrad.

453
00:25:52,985 --> 00:25:54,751
Conrad and Ben.

454
00:26:02,628 --> 00:26:05,596
And there's the library.

455
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:10,100
That's Gordon Kellogg's Supply.

456
00:26:10,169 --> 00:26:13,437
Oh, that's a...
nice looking store.

457
00:26:13,506 --> 00:26:15,472
Sell lumber...
What else they sell?

458
00:26:15,541 --> 00:26:16,606
Whatever you need.

459
00:26:16,675 --> 00:26:17,707
Oh, nice.

460
00:26:17,776 --> 00:26:19,910
And there's your basic house.

461
00:26:19,979 --> 00:26:21,857
Uh-huh. And...

462
00:26:21,881 --> 00:26:23,881
as you can see, woods.

463
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,815
Yeah.

464
00:26:25,885 --> 00:26:27,551
You like it here, huh?

465
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:29,452
Yeah. Yeah.

466
00:26:29,521 --> 00:26:31,421
It's pretty much all I know.

467
00:26:31,490 --> 00:26:33,190
I've traveled.

468
00:26:33,259 --> 00:26:35,169
You know, I've been
to New York, Miami...

469
00:26:35,193 --> 00:26:36,193
Atlanta?

470
00:26:36,228 --> 00:26:37,728
Been to Atlanta.

471
00:26:37,796 --> 00:26:39,930
But I always wind up back here.

472
00:26:39,998 --> 00:26:41,031
Well,

473
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:42,499
you like here.

474
00:26:42,568 --> 00:26:44,200
You like your job.

475
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:45,402
Yeah.

476
00:26:45,471 --> 00:26:47,370
I think I'm ahead of the game.

477
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:49,172
Yeah.

478
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:56,213
Okay, here we are.

479
00:27:15,234 --> 00:27:18,202
Boy, that's nice!

480
00:27:18,270 --> 00:27:20,204
Big.

481
00:27:20,272 --> 00:27:22,840
Sure doesn't look
like a time-share.

482
00:27:22,908 --> 00:27:24,886
Oh, time-share?

483
00:27:24,910 --> 00:27:27,477
No, Mr. Bartell
owned this place.

484
00:27:27,546 --> 00:27:29,412
Paid cash for it.

485
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,414
Cash? Yeah.

486
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:33,416
He stay here by himself?

487
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:34,562
Sometimes.

488
00:27:34,586 --> 00:27:36,220
A lot of times.

489
00:27:36,288 --> 00:27:38,734
Then a lot of times he'd
bring the family along.

490
00:27:38,758 --> 00:27:43,693
And... then, a lot of times he'd
come down here with another woman.

491
00:27:43,763 --> 00:27:45,273
Yeah? Yeah.

492
00:27:45,297 --> 00:27:46,663
Oh, yeah.

493
00:27:46,732 --> 00:27:48,165
He had several.

494
00:27:48,234 --> 00:27:50,378
Blondes, brunettes, redheads.

495
00:27:50,402 --> 00:27:53,536
I mean, me, I just
got one, you know?

496
00:27:53,605 --> 00:27:56,640
Yeah, me, too.

497
00:27:58,210 --> 00:28:01,278
Do all his friends have
homes as nice as this?

498
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:02,545
Oh, yeah.

499
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:04,281
Huh.

500
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:07,450
You have any idea
what they do for a living?

501
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:10,821
Well, I'm pretty sure
they're not deputy sheriffs.

502
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:13,171
Yeah.

503
00:28:16,328 --> 00:28:17,761
Huh.

504
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:21,464
How long these fellas
been coming down here?

505
00:28:21,534 --> 00:28:23,578
Oh, about five years, I guess.

506
00:28:23,602 --> 00:28:25,669
Huh.

507
00:28:25,738 --> 00:28:27,004
Mm.

508
00:28:28,874 --> 00:28:30,841
Oh, yeah.

509
00:28:43,122 --> 00:28:45,055
Duck hunters, huh?

510
00:28:45,124 --> 00:28:46,368
Yes, sir.

511
00:28:46,392 --> 00:28:47,624
Uh-huh.

512
00:28:49,661 --> 00:28:51,427
They any good?

513
00:28:51,497 --> 00:28:53,741
They brag about it, give
game to the locals sometimes,

514
00:28:53,765 --> 00:28:55,544
but I don't know if
they're any good.

515
00:28:55,568 --> 00:28:57,968
Do you know anybody who would?

516
00:28:58,037 --> 00:28:59,747
Are you kidding?
To hear them talk,

517
00:28:59,771 --> 00:29:01,750
they've bagged every
duck they ever shot at.

518
00:29:01,774 --> 00:29:04,285
Huh. Did you ever
go hunting with them?

519
00:29:04,309 --> 00:29:06,442
Nah. They keep pretty
much to themselves.

520
00:29:06,511 --> 00:29:09,045
But the town folks love
'em, don't they, Conrad?

521
00:29:09,114 --> 00:29:11,025
Yeah, they get
along with everybody.

522
00:29:11,049 --> 00:29:13,316
Give to charities in
town, different causes.

523
00:29:13,385 --> 00:29:14,550
Huh.

524
00:29:14,619 --> 00:29:16,765
Do they come in here a lot?

525
00:29:16,789 --> 00:29:18,655
A lot. Have a couple beers,

526
00:29:18,723 --> 00:29:22,092
and then either eat dinner
here or go to one of their houses

527
00:29:22,161 --> 00:29:24,261
to play poker and
have pizzas delivered.

528
00:29:24,330 --> 00:29:27,097
They play... poker a lot?

529
00:29:27,166 --> 00:29:29,065
Well, uh...

530
00:29:29,134 --> 00:29:32,335
they like to gamble
a little, I guess.

531
00:29:32,404 --> 00:29:34,938
Sometimes the hunters run into
what you call "bluebird weather."

532
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:36,839
Clear days without any wind.

533
00:29:36,909 --> 00:29:39,910
Ducks don't fly at all, so
might as well play poker.

534
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:45,348
Yeah, in-in the daytime,
but at-at night, I...

535
00:29:45,417 --> 00:29:48,796
Well, I guess if you
hunt long enough,

536
00:29:48,820 --> 00:29:52,422
you get to knowing when
bluebird weather's coming.

537
00:29:59,865 --> 00:30:01,943
<i>Huh. What?</i>

538
00:30:01,967 --> 00:30:04,568
This is a peculiar
bunch of duck hunters.

539
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:06,803
Play poker all night, eat pizza.

540
00:30:06,872 --> 00:30:08,939
What happens to
the duck they shoot?

541
00:30:09,007 --> 00:30:10,774
Don't they eat 'em?

542
00:30:10,843 --> 00:30:12,921
Maybe they don't like duck.

543
00:30:12,945 --> 00:30:15,578
Like to shoot 'em;
don't like to eat 'em.

544
00:30:15,648 --> 00:30:18,515
<i>Give 'em away...
Lot of people do that.</i>

545
00:30:18,583 --> 00:30:20,984
<i>Something is wrong.</i>

546
00:30:21,053 --> 00:30:24,721
Central dispatch to
McMasters. Can you copy?

547
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:26,089
Go ahead, Clarence.

548
00:30:26,158 --> 00:30:27,824
Conrad.

549
00:30:27,893 --> 00:30:29,626
Go ahead, Clarence.

550
00:30:29,695 --> 00:30:30,761
Conrad?

551
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:32,109
What?!

552
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:34,142
You better get over
to Jack Rose's garage.

553
00:30:34,166 --> 00:30:35,432
Spencer Hamilton's there,

554
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:38,101
and he's trying to beat
the living hell out of Jack.

555
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:39,281
Great.

556
00:30:43,875 --> 00:30:46,776
Do you suppose I could
just rent a car down here?

557
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:48,022
Oh, yeah!

558
00:30:50,850 --> 00:30:53,016
Leave me alone... I
don't have to talk to you.

559
00:30:53,085 --> 00:30:54,262
Will you stand still?

560
00:30:54,286 --> 00:30:56,664
Come here! Just-just
tell me why you lied.

561
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:58,322
Get out of here!

562
00:30:58,390 --> 00:31:00,190
Come here!

563
00:31:00,259 --> 00:31:01,903
You're a damn liar, Rose!

564
00:31:01,927 --> 00:31:03,726
Come back here!

565
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,978
You better get out of here!

566
00:31:10,002 --> 00:31:11,282
The cops are coming!

567
00:31:22,081 --> 00:31:23,680
Get out of here!

568
00:31:23,749 --> 00:31:25,182
Leave me alone!

569
00:31:25,251 --> 00:31:27,417
Tell me why you lied!

570
00:31:31,823 --> 00:31:33,757
Open the door, Rose.

571
00:31:35,827 --> 00:31:37,761
Come on out of there, Rose!

572
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:39,595
Come on out of there!

573
00:31:39,665 --> 00:31:41,142
Tell me why you lied?

574
00:31:41,166 --> 00:31:43,099
Come on out of there, Rose.

575
00:31:44,836 --> 00:31:46,848
In another minute, I'll be
through this door, Rose.

576
00:31:46,872 --> 00:31:48,482
You are some kind of maniac!

577
00:31:48,506 --> 00:31:51,466
It's just gonna be
you and me, Rose.

578
00:31:53,011 --> 00:31:55,578
Get out of here!

579
00:31:55,647 --> 00:31:56,857
Almost there, Rose!

580
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:58,648
Hey, Spence! Hold it!

581
00:31:58,717 --> 00:31:59,916
Okay!

582
00:31:59,985 --> 00:32:02,185
Okay, okay.

583
00:32:02,254 --> 00:32:04,588
Jack, come on out of there.

584
00:32:07,793 --> 00:32:09,692
Jack! Come on

585
00:32:09,762 --> 00:32:10,894
out of there.

586
00:32:10,963 --> 00:32:12,929
He's not gonna hurt you.

587
00:32:15,734 --> 00:32:17,033
See that?

588
00:32:17,102 --> 00:32:19,147
He tried to kill me! I'm trying

589
00:32:19,171 --> 00:32:21,171
to make you tell
me why you lied.

590
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:23,005
I'm gonna press charges, pal.

591
00:32:23,074 --> 00:32:25,775
They're gonna electrocute
you for killing Ryan Bartell,

592
00:32:25,844 --> 00:32:27,677
and they're gonna
electrocute you again

593
00:32:27,746 --> 00:32:29,713
for trying to kill me!

594
00:32:29,782 --> 00:32:31,214
Uh, Mr. Rose,

595
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:33,950
you<i> can</i> file charges,

596
00:32:34,019 --> 00:32:38,087
but if you do, then
everybody's gonna wonder

597
00:32:38,156 --> 00:32:41,825
what you did to make
Spencer so mad at you.

598
00:32:41,894 --> 00:32:44,827
You just keep him away from me.

599
00:32:46,831 --> 00:32:48,765
You think he can do that?

600
00:32:48,834 --> 00:32:51,034
Count on it.

601
00:32:51,103 --> 00:32:52,835
All right, then it's over.

602
00:32:54,907 --> 00:32:56,106
Come on, Jack.

603
00:32:56,174 --> 00:32:57,573
Come on.

604
00:33:02,747 --> 00:33:04,781
Now, I told you,

605
00:33:04,850 --> 00:33:07,583
and I'm gonna tell
you one more time,

606
00:33:07,653 --> 00:33:09,752
don't ever try
something like this again.

607
00:33:09,822 --> 00:33:11,166
But he... You're on trial

608
00:33:11,190 --> 00:33:12,589
for murder!

609
00:33:12,658 --> 00:33:15,825
You can't go around here
acting like some kind of a jackass.

610
00:33:15,894 --> 00:33:18,395
Hell... You got that?

611
00:33:19,765 --> 00:33:21,565
Yeah, I got that.

612
00:33:21,633 --> 00:33:24,534
Good. 'Cause otherwise,
you're digging your own grave.

613
00:33:24,603 --> 00:33:26,669
And with the
evidence against you,

614
00:33:26,738 --> 00:33:29,139
it won't take much of a shovel.

615
00:33:54,533 --> 00:33:55,798
Hi.

616
00:33:55,868 --> 00:33:58,568
You scared the hell out of me!

617
00:33:58,637 --> 00:34:00,570
Oh, I'm sorry. The
door was open.

618
00:34:00,639 --> 00:34:03,140
Uh, Mr. D'Amato?

619
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,707
Yeah?

620
00:34:04,776 --> 00:34:08,111
I'm, uh, I'm Ben Matlock,
Spencer Hamilton's lawyer.

621
00:34:08,180 --> 00:34:09,579
He's a bum.

622
00:34:09,648 --> 00:34:11,681
He shot Ryan
Bartell in cold blood.

623
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:13,617
Is that right? Yeah.

624
00:34:13,685 --> 00:34:15,952
Hm. What's that?

625
00:34:17,189 --> 00:34:18,888
It's mousse.

626
00:34:18,957 --> 00:34:21,491
Chocolate mousse. Mm.

627
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:22,925
What's that?

628
00:34:22,994 --> 00:34:25,262
Spaghetti sauce.

629
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:26,929
Green spaghetti sauce?

630
00:34:26,998 --> 00:34:28,331
It's pesto.

631
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:30,667
This...

632
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:33,069
nice glass of wine,
a little mousse,

633
00:34:33,138 --> 00:34:35,138
you forget about Heaven.

634
00:34:35,207 --> 00:34:37,106
Oh, that's right.

635
00:34:37,176 --> 00:34:39,909
You own a restaurant
in Boston, don't you?

636
00:34:39,978 --> 00:34:41,744
Yeah. Oh.

637
00:34:42,981 --> 00:34:44,648
This is nice here.

638
00:34:44,716 --> 00:34:46,394
Uh...

639
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:48,985
you and your friends
bring your, uh...

640
00:34:49,054 --> 00:34:50,987
uh, families down here, do you?

641
00:34:51,056 --> 00:34:53,122
Yeah. They enjoy it.

642
00:34:53,191 --> 00:34:54,469
Uh,

643
00:34:54,493 --> 00:34:56,559
sometimes you don't?

644
00:34:56,628 --> 00:34:57,827
Yeah.

645
00:34:57,896 --> 00:35:01,064
Wha-What's wrong with that?

646
00:35:01,133 --> 00:35:03,065
Sometimes you
bring another woman?

647
00:35:03,135 --> 00:35:04,646
Who told you that? Oh,

648
00:35:04,670 --> 00:35:05,735
I just heard it.

649
00:35:05,804 --> 00:35:07,236
Let me tell you something,

650
00:35:07,306 --> 00:35:09,773
I don't bother nobody;
nobody bothers me.

651
00:35:09,842 --> 00:35:13,810
Something wrong with the gun?

652
00:35:13,879 --> 00:35:15,545
Oh, no.

653
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:17,492
No, it's a nice
gun... it's just...

654
00:35:17,516 --> 00:35:19,782
a little dirty.

655
00:35:24,890 --> 00:35:27,023
This shot, uh, is illegal.

656
00:35:27,092 --> 00:35:29,337
It's lead... you're
supposed to use

657
00:35:29,361 --> 00:35:30,861
steel shot over water.

658
00:35:30,929 --> 00:35:32,162
Federal law.

659
00:35:32,231 --> 00:35:34,231
Oh, yeah.

660
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:38,067
Yeah, I-I have to get
some next season.

661
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:40,036
Talking about...

662
00:35:40,105 --> 00:35:41,804
how, uh...

663
00:35:41,874 --> 00:35:48,378
Spencer Hamilton shot
Ryan Bartell in cold blood,

664
00:35:48,447 --> 00:35:50,190
where were you that morning?

665
00:35:50,214 --> 00:35:52,381
Are we gonna have
to go through this?

666
00:35:52,451 --> 00:35:54,083
Can't get around it.

667
00:35:54,153 --> 00:35:55,952
I was here.

668
00:35:56,021 --> 00:35:57,386
Asleep.

669
00:35:57,456 --> 00:35:59,723
Your mousse is burning.

670
00:35:59,791 --> 00:36:00,923
Damn!

671
00:36:03,829 --> 00:36:07,030
Enjoyed talking with you.

672
00:36:15,073 --> 00:36:16,205
Yeah, it's me.

673
00:36:16,274 --> 00:36:18,353
I just got a visit from
that lawyer, Matlock.

674
00:36:18,377 --> 00:36:21,244
I took the wrong door.

675
00:36:21,312 --> 00:36:22,478
Went in the toilet.

676
00:36:30,222 --> 00:36:32,288
He's going to be a problem.

677
00:36:57,982 --> 00:37:00,250
Excuse me.

678
00:37:00,318 --> 00:37:01,817
Is there something
I can do for you?

679
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,831
Oh, hi. Uh, I'm Ben Matlock,

680
00:37:03,855 --> 00:37:05,500
Spencer Hamilton's lawyer.

681
00:37:05,524 --> 00:37:06,923
That's a nice boat.

682
00:37:06,991 --> 00:37:08,824
I like it. Yeah.

683
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:12,262
So, you're a stock
broker from-from Chicago?

684
00:37:12,330 --> 00:37:13,896
Yes.

685
00:37:13,965 --> 00:37:16,933
Do you folks up there
know something we don't?

686
00:37:17,001 --> 00:37:18,968
Well, we just know it first.

687
00:37:19,037 --> 00:37:23,273
What I meant was,
uh, that flat-bottom boat

688
00:37:23,341 --> 00:37:24,919
that's on the
trailer right there?

689
00:37:24,943 --> 00:37:26,709
How do you haul that

690
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:30,313
when you don't have a
trailer hitch on your car?

691
00:37:30,381 --> 00:37:33,316
Oh, there's one
on the other car.

692
00:37:33,384 --> 00:37:35,897
I heard you always
drive that sports car

693
00:37:35,921 --> 00:37:37,164
when you're down here.

694
00:37:37,188 --> 00:37:39,300
He sold his other car to me.

695
00:37:39,324 --> 00:37:41,169
I buy all my cars
from my friends.

696
00:37:41,193 --> 00:37:42,270
That way, I know
what I'm getting.

697
00:37:42,294 --> 00:37:43,959
What a good idea!

698
00:37:44,028 --> 00:37:46,563
Ben Matlock, Spencer
Hamilton's lawyer.

699
00:37:46,632 --> 00:37:47,664
You must be Lee Kramer.

700
00:37:47,733 --> 00:37:48,664
That's right.

701
00:37:48,734 --> 00:37:50,332
Ah.

702
00:37:50,402 --> 00:37:52,301
Get your gun, David.

703
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:53,570
Let's go shoot some targets.

704
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:55,137
How about me?

705
00:37:55,207 --> 00:37:57,740
I mean, you got your headset.

706
00:37:57,809 --> 00:37:59,153
You can listen to some Mozart,

707
00:37:59,177 --> 00:38:00,521
or the Grateful
Dead, or something.

708
00:38:00,545 --> 00:38:02,612
But, uh, I'm not doing anything.

709
00:38:02,681 --> 00:38:03,846
So, what do you say?

710
00:38:03,915 --> 00:38:06,682
Okay. Yeah.

711
00:38:19,564 --> 00:38:21,898
So, are you and David
both stock brokers?

712
00:38:21,967 --> 00:38:24,567
Hell, no. I'm in oil leasing.

713
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:27,704
Oh. Dallas? Denver? Houston?

714
00:38:27,773 --> 00:38:29,239
Houston.

715
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:31,507
Oh. That's an easy
way to lose your shirt,

716
00:38:31,576 --> 00:38:32,608
especially these days.

717
00:38:34,012 --> 00:38:35,422
Awful lot of bad
luck going around.

718
00:38:35,446 --> 00:38:37,747
Yeah.

719
00:38:39,384 --> 00:38:41,817
Ooh.

720
00:38:41,887 --> 00:38:44,754
You want to survive, you
got to know what you're doing.

721
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:47,924
Yeah. Could I, uh, take a look?

722
00:38:47,993 --> 00:38:49,259
Sure.

723
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:52,228
Thanks.

724
00:38:52,297 --> 00:38:54,130
Hey, that's nice.

725
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:55,431
Take a shot.

726
00:38:55,500 --> 00:38:56,766
Oh, no.

727
00:38:56,835 --> 00:38:58,802
I wouldn't be able
to hit anything.

728
00:38:58,870 --> 00:39:02,605
Boy, your gun is clean.
Your hunting buddies

729
00:39:02,674 --> 00:39:04,807
could take lessons from you.

730
00:39:04,876 --> 00:39:06,754
Ernie D'Amato's
gun's dirty, rusty.

731
00:39:06,778 --> 00:39:08,010
So's Ryan's.

732
00:39:08,080 --> 00:39:10,813
City boys. What
can you do, right?

733
00:39:10,882 --> 00:39:12,093
Yeah.

734
00:39:12,117 --> 00:39:15,851
Uh, were you shooting the
morning Ryan was killed?

735
00:39:15,921 --> 00:39:17,954
At 6:00?

736
00:39:19,257 --> 00:39:21,157
I was asleep.

737
00:39:22,828 --> 00:39:25,228
At home. Alone.

738
00:39:29,634 --> 00:39:31,545
Look, if I'd have
killed Ryan Bartell,

739
00:39:31,569 --> 00:39:34,304
I wouldn't have needed two
shots to bring him down, you know?

740
00:39:34,373 --> 00:39:37,206
Well, you got a point.

741
00:39:47,085 --> 00:39:48,918
Oh!

742
00:39:48,987 --> 00:39:51,620
There you go.

743
00:40:11,543 --> 00:40:13,843
Hey.

744
00:40:13,912 --> 00:40:15,277
Boy!

745
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:17,906
There's a lot of
people down here.

746
00:40:17,949 --> 00:40:19,882
Summer time. They
come from all over.

747
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:25,521
Well, I-I don't blame them.

748
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:27,890
It's pretty down here.

749
00:40:27,959 --> 00:40:30,760
Have, uh, have you
been here all your life?

750
00:40:30,829 --> 00:40:33,095
Like the fella says, not yet.

751
00:40:39,971 --> 00:40:41,571
What do you think?

752
00:40:41,639 --> 00:40:43,205
Afraid I'm past it.

753
00:40:45,076 --> 00:40:46,254
Do you remember?

754
00:40:46,278 --> 00:40:48,878
Fondly.

755
00:40:48,947 --> 00:40:52,548
Sheriff, those,
uh, those fellas,

756
00:40:52,617 --> 00:40:54,495
those hunting fellas...

757
00:40:54,519 --> 00:40:57,287
uh, how did they
get to be friends?

758
00:40:57,355 --> 00:40:59,566
I mean, uh, one's from Houston.

759
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:00,734
One's from Boston.

760
00:41:00,758 --> 00:41:02,458
One's from Chicago.

761
00:41:02,527 --> 00:41:03,938
I mean, they're from all over.

762
00:41:03,962 --> 00:41:06,196
Well, the story is,
they met on vacation,

763
00:41:06,264 --> 00:41:07,363
liked one another,

764
00:41:07,432 --> 00:41:09,732
and they started
meeting at different places

765
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:11,078
and taking little trips together

766
00:41:11,102 --> 00:41:12,535
and wound up here.

767
00:41:12,603 --> 00:41:14,937
Huh. Wound up here.

768
00:41:15,006 --> 00:41:16,472
Sheriff! Mr. Matlock!

769
00:41:16,541 --> 00:41:17,473
Hello, Commissioner.

770
00:41:17,542 --> 00:41:19,675
Oh. Mr. Lilley.

771
00:41:19,744 --> 00:41:21,288
What they say about you is true.

772
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,556
You are everywhere.

773
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:24,013
I like to keep up.

774
00:41:24,082 --> 00:41:25,848
But you? You're the
one that's everywhere.

775
00:41:25,917 --> 00:41:27,328
Oh... Isn't he, Sheriff?

776
00:41:27,352 --> 00:41:29,385
Uh, he's a little young, yet.

777
00:41:29,454 --> 00:41:30,619
See you later, boys.

778
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:31,968
See you, Sheriff.

779
00:41:32,023 --> 00:41:33,356
I heard you was over here.

780
00:41:33,425 --> 00:41:36,025
You, uh, making any
progress on your case?

781
00:41:36,094 --> 00:41:39,828
Oh, you know, asking
a few questions around.

782
00:41:39,897 --> 00:41:42,998
So, uh, county
commissioner, huh?

783
00:41:43,068 --> 00:41:44,200
Oh, no, no.

784
00:41:44,269 --> 00:41:46,069
I've run for commissioner
a lot of times.

785
00:41:46,137 --> 00:41:47,281
Never won?

786
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:48,538
Never did.

787
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:50,617
Pretty soon, folks just started
calling me "Commissioner."

788
00:41:50,641 --> 00:41:51,919
Oh.

789
00:41:51,943 --> 00:41:53,309
Ex-officio, huh?

790
00:41:53,378 --> 00:41:54,922
Yeah. Hell, I like a good joke.

791
00:41:54,946 --> 00:41:56,112
Yeah.

792
00:41:56,181 --> 00:41:58,747
But in the meantime,
I got my little practice,

793
00:41:58,816 --> 00:42:00,216
insurance business,

794
00:42:00,285 --> 00:42:01,695
one-third interest
in a used car lot.

795
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:03,018
Huh.

796
00:42:03,088 --> 00:42:04,665
So, you making some
progress on that case, huh?

797
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:07,523
Well, yeah. Moderate, moderate.

798
00:42:20,238 --> 00:42:22,572
Ben Matlock.

799
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:25,141
Who is this?

800
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:27,276
Elizabethan Gardens?

801
00:42:27,345 --> 00:42:29,278
Well, I guess so, but...

802
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:26,068
♪ ♪

803
00:43:42,988 --> 00:43:44,920
♪ ♪

804
00:43:58,636 --> 00:43:59,916
What's going on?

805
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:01,571
I got a call, anonymous.

806
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,405
Uh, a person fitting
your description

807
00:44:03,474 --> 00:44:06,609
was seen buying or
accepting a substance

808
00:44:06,678 --> 00:44:08,911
at Whalebone
Junction on the beach.

809
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:11,113
And they said this
car was here, too.

810
00:44:13,585 --> 00:44:17,152
Well, you don't think
I got dope in my car?

811
00:44:17,221 --> 00:44:19,188
Well, I doubt it,
and I hope not,

812
00:44:19,256 --> 00:44:22,892
but I'm going to have to ask
you to open your car, Mr. Matlock.

813
00:44:22,961 --> 00:44:24,694
Well...

814
00:44:24,762 --> 00:44:26,929
Well, that...

815
00:44:26,998 --> 00:44:29,565
This just caps this day.

816
00:44:29,634 --> 00:44:31,767
Hey.

817
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:33,803
Sorry, but, uh,

818
00:44:33,871 --> 00:44:35,771
