knock your hat off.

1025
00:53:24,001 --> 00:53:25,178
What? Well,

1026
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:26,668
I got me an idea.

1027
00:53:26,737 --> 00:53:28,615
I just had to follow
through on it. What?

1028
00:53:28,639 --> 00:53:30,805
Well, you know
Jack Rose's garage?

1029
00:53:30,874 --> 00:53:32,085
Yeah. Yeah.

1030
00:53:32,109 --> 00:53:35,177
This fellow works there...
Ned... Ned, uh Porter.

1031
00:53:35,246 --> 00:53:37,779
Yeah. And, uh, he pumps gas,

1032
00:53:37,848 --> 00:53:40,215
checks oil, water,
tires, stuff like that.

1033
00:53:40,284 --> 00:53:41,395
Yeah. Yeah.

1034
00:53:41,419 --> 00:53:43,785
Well, I went there,
and I got me some gas,

1035
00:53:43,854 --> 00:53:46,388
and I got my oil
checked, water, tires,

1036
00:53:46,457 --> 00:53:48,001
stuff like that. Uh-huh.

1037
00:53:48,025 --> 00:53:49,025
All right, okay, okay.

1038
00:53:49,093 --> 00:53:50,159
Anyway, I know Ned.

1039
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:51,604
Yeah. See? See?

1040
00:53:51,628 --> 00:53:53,728
Ned likes to talk.

1041
00:53:53,797 --> 00:53:55,163
Yeah?

1042
00:53:55,233 --> 00:53:58,066
The money for Jack
Rose's garage was put up

1043
00:53:58,135 --> 00:54:02,070
by Lee Kramer, David
Channing, Ernie D'Amato

1044
00:54:02,139 --> 00:54:05,340
and the late Frank
Hamilton and Ryan Bartell.

1045
00:54:22,226 --> 00:54:24,560
It's beautiful.

1046
00:54:24,629 --> 00:54:26,729
Mm.

1047
00:54:26,797 --> 00:54:28,731
Sure is.

1048
00:54:38,743 --> 00:54:40,476
Here's to...

1049
00:54:40,544 --> 00:54:42,144
new friends.

1050
00:54:51,022 --> 00:54:53,188
How about a walk on the beach?

1051
00:54:53,257 --> 00:54:54,823
Yeah.

1052
00:54:54,892 --> 00:54:57,259
Uh, expecting a phone call.

1053
00:54:57,327 --> 00:54:59,194
Business.

1054
00:54:59,263 --> 00:55:00,495
Oh.

1055
00:55:00,564 --> 00:55:02,497
